<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad al-Sanusi of Dar al-Kuti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1911</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad al-Sanusi of Dar al-Kuti was sultan of Dar al-Kuti, in what is now the north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a>, from 1890 to 1911. Installed with the backing of the warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabih-az-zubayr">Rabih az-Zubayr</a>, he built a fortified capital at Ndele from 1896 and raided the lands to the south for slaves, trading them and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> north to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a>. He signed treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> but was killed by French forces in 1911.</p></div>
